SUMMARY:Downtown Asheville Scavenger Hunt 2.0
DESCRIPTION:Friendly People in Asheville\nIt’s spring\, y’all\, so it
 ’s time for **Downtown Asheville Scavenger Hunt 2.0**. 🎉\n\nSame fun 
 hunt\, all new clues. Whether you joined our hunt last fall or are brand n
 ew to the game\, come out and give it a try! This is a fun way to explore 
 Asheville and make new friends.\n\nHere’s how it works:\n\nWe will gathe
 r at the S&W Market at 56 Patton Avenue at 2:30pm. We’ll hang out upstai
 rs — at Periscope — and get snacks and drinks\, etc. If you’re a lit
 tle late\, no worries.\n\nWe will break up into teams and go over the rule
 s at 3:15pm. Teams will have 10-15 minutes to review the clues\, and the h
 unt will begin at 3:30pm.\n\nTeams will have an hour to hunt for 40 clues 
 scattered across downtown and take a selfie with each clue. \\*Bonus point
 s for taking a selfie with the clue and a willing stranger. More willing s
 trangers = more points.\\*\n\nThe hunt ends at 4:30pm back at Periscope in
  the S&W.\n\nIt will take 20-30 minutes to review all the teams’ answers
  and determine the winner.\nThe prize will be the glory of winning! 🏆\n
 That said\, this hunt’s 40th question is a diabolical bonus question wit
 h only one correct answer. Get it right\, and I’ll buy you (and everyone
  on your team) a drink.\n\n**What to bring:**\n\n* Walking or running shoe
 s (the hunt spans from South Slope to the north end of downtown)\n* Your p
 hone for taking pics\n* A pencil or pen to mark off clues as you find them
 \n* Your competitive spirit!\n\n**Parking:**\nParking is available nearby 
 at the Rankin (68 Rankin Ave) and Wall Street (45 Wall Street) parking dec
 ks\, as well as at the Coxe Ave Garage (52 Coxe Ave). Metered street parki
 ng is also available around the corner on Church Street.\n\n**Disclaimer a
 nd Release of Liability:**\nParticipants are responsible for their safety.
  If you sign up or participate in this event\, you acknowledge that you fr
 eely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, a
 nd damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this event.
 \n\nLooking forward to seeing y’all there!
